Aim-
Demonstrate use of object- oriented programming concepts

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Create a class named Student
3. Define method getdata()
        . Input USN
        . Input Name
        . Input marks for 5 subjects (marks1, marks2, marks3, marks4, marks5)
4. Define method total_marks()
        . Calculate total marks
          total = marks1 + marks2 + marks3 + marks4 + marks5
5. Define method display()
        . Print student name
        . Print USN
        . Print total marks
6. Create an object of class Student
7. Call getdata() method
        . Accept input values from user
8. Call total_marks() method
        . Compute total marks
9. Call display() method
        . Display the student details and total marks
10. Stop

Code:-
class Student:
    def getdata(self):
        self.USN = input("Enter the USN:")
        self.name = input("Enter the name:")
        self.marks1 = int(input("Enter marks 1:"))
        self.marks2 = int(input("Enter marks 2:"))
        self.marks3 = int(input("Enter marks 3:"))
        self.marks4 = int(input("Enter marks 4:"))
        self.marks5 = int(input("Enter marks 5:"))

    def total_marks(self):
        self.total = (self.marks1 + self.marks2 + self.marks3 + self.marks4 + self.marks5)

    def display(self):
        print("\n Student Details")
        print("Name : ", self.name)
        print("USN  : ", self.USN)
        print("Total marks : ", self.total)

obj = Student()
obj.getdata()
obj.total_marks()
obj.display()

